      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright© Acta Chirurgica Belgica.",
        "AbstractText": "Primary presacral adenocarcinoma is a rare presacral lesion. We report a 36-year-old male patient with -primary presacral adenocarcinoma. The patient presented with a six-month history of sacrococcygeal pain. MRI demonstrated a 4×3 cm2, well-defined presacral mass. He underwent a parasacrococcygeal procedure with complete resection of the -tumor, which subsequent histology showed adenocarcinoma. At 15 months follow-up, he remains disease free."
      },
